+## Photo authenticity checks (C2PA reading + metadata consistency)
+Added on top of the sealed capture. It is **derived and re-runnable**, stored in `evidence_photo_authenticity` (one row per capture), and deliberately **not** sealed in the hash chain: the chain commits to bytes, times and source; this is an opinion computed by versioned code (`ANALYZER_VERSION`).
+
+**Flow.** UI button → edge action `analyze_authenticity` → capture read under the caller's JWT (RLS: account + job visibility) → original re-downloaded and re-hashed against the sealed `original_sha256` (mismatch = 422, nothing stored) → `analyzePhotoAuthenticity()` → service-role `evp_store_authenticity()`. An up-to-date stored report is returned without recomputation; a new analyzer version recomputes. Checks run only on request. Results appear in the job's dispute evidence panel and in the warranty claim packet (`PhotoAuthenticityPanel`).
+
+**C2PA (read only).** Parsed with `@contentauth/c2pa-wasm` (pinned `0.13.4`, MIT, Content Authenticity Initiative). Nothing is signed. Reported separately: validation (valid / invalid), signer trust, declared actions, declared generated/synthetic media.
+
+**Metadata consistency.** A bounded in-repo parser reads EXIF/XMP/dimensions (JPEG, PNG, WebP). Heuristics produce a **confidence 0-100 with reasons**, or `insufficient` (no number) when nothing reliable can be compared. It is never a verdict, the UI says so, and the copy avoids "authentic", "fake" and "forged". Weights live in `heuristics.ts` (`WEIGHTS`).
+
+### Limits of the authenticity checks (read before relying on them)
+- **Not a forgery detector.** A high number means "nothing here contradicts the capture record", not "genuine". A low number means "look closer", not "edited". EXIF/XMP can be rewritten by anyone, so metadata that agrees is weak evidence; this cannot detect a careful forgery that also rewrites metadata, nor AI-generated or screen-recaptured images that carry no tell-tale metadata.
+- **Weights are judgement, not statistics.** They have not been calibrated on real data (no labelled corpus, false-positive/false-negative rates unknown). Treat the number as an ordering aid. **[VERIFY]** before quoting it to a third party; **[COUNSEL]** before using it as evidence in a formal proceeding.
+- **Absence proves nothing.** Messaging apps, screenshots and the in-app camera (which re-encodes at quality 85 / 2048 px) strip EXIF and C2PA. "No metadata" is reported as information, and as `insufficient` when it is all there is.
+- **C2PA validity is not trust.** "Valid" means the signed claim is intact and the file matches what was signed. Without trust anchors (`C2PA_TRUST_ANCHORS_PEM`, public certificates, operator supplied) the signer is reported as **not evaluated**, never as verified. Vireek does not bundle a trust list; obtain the current list from the C2PA conformance programme **[VERIFY]**. A valid manifest can still declare edits or generated media, and the signer's claim is only as good as the signer.
+- **Clocks.** EXIF time has no zone unless `OffsetTime*` exists; the comparison infers a plausible zone and tolerates ambiguity, and device time can be wrong or spoofed. The job-window check uses job timestamps as recorded.
+- **Size and formats.** C2PA is skipped above 12 MB (edge CPU budget). HEIC is detected and C2PA-read, but its EXIF/XMP is not parsed.
+- **Privacy.** GPS is reported as present/absent only; coordinates, serial numbers, names, comments and thumbnails are never extracted or stored. The original file itself may contain a location: consider that before sharing it. Results are not exposed on public verification links and are not added to the text inserted into dispute explanations, so a reviewer cannot mistake a heuristic for a sealed fact.
+- **Runtime [VERIFY].** The WASM asset is read at start-up through `import.meta.resolve`. This works under Deno locally; it has not been verified on the hosted Supabase edge runtime. If it fails, C2PA is reported as `unavailable` and metadata checks still run.
+
 ## Location privacy
 Coordinates are stored only in `evidence_photo_locations` (no policy, no grants: unreadable to clients) and never in the chain. The chain holds a **salted commitment**; deleting the row (purge/retention) destroys the salt, so the chain stays valid and the commitment links to nothing.
 A coordinate is accepted only if **all** hold: account switch `evidence_photo_policies.capture_location`; `location_privacy_policies.require_consent = true` and `location_tracking_gate()` = `allowed` for the technician; photo device time within `arrived_at|started_at − 15 min … completed_at|now + 60 min`. Otherwise coordinates are discarded and the reason is recorded (`no_consent`, `off_duty`, `outside_job_window`, …). Rounded to 4 decimals (~11 m). Managers only can read coordinates (`evp_coordinates`).
